    {
      "id": "28bcf76a-861f-4e96-b84d-89393dc19fe2",
      "name": "Why MCP is awesome: one protocol, every tool",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Why MCP is awesome: one protocol, every tool",
      "docTypeId": "c7a5b5dd-fafc-4c11-ac4e-14a8e7bfddb6",
      "templateId": "1b139464-b8d3-4af9-bb18-32444b276563",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "title",
          "value": "Why MCP is awesome: one protocol, every tool"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.DateTime",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "publishDate",
          "value": "2026-10-01 09:00:00"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "excerpt",
          "value": "Before MCP, every AI integration was a one-off. Now a single open protocol lets any assistant talk to any tool."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "listingImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "b1c0f6a2-3d54-4e0b-9a1e-5f7c2d8e4a01",
              "mediaKey": "8791b03a-e349-4e40-bd6d-d7af04f79e3f",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "body",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "d8ea5283-f2de-4281-9241-c0173c057ac2",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "6c18757c-8a2a-452c-9136-b9b25eff8550",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "dc6b448f-d52c-4b81-90bd-d52fa8b7cd60",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "ed84097c-6e76-40cd-9bf5-e92ff46571f7",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "25b8da17-11eb-42e9-80f2-0df90950e32f",
                "key": "d8ea5283-f2de-4281-9241-c0173c057ac2",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "content",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<h2>The integration problem</h2><p>For years, connecting an AI assistant to a real system meant writing a bespoke integration: a custom plugin here, a hand-rolled API wrapper there. Every assistant needed its own adapter for every tool, and every adapter broke whenever either side changed.</p><p>The Model Context Protocol (MCP) replaces that tangle with a single open standard. A tool describes what it can do once, and any MCP-aware assistant can discover and use it.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "f772eec5-bfe2-44ca-844a-a1fecadfeed2",
                "key": "6c18757c-8a2a-452c-9136-b9b25eff8550",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "d3e2b8c4-5f76-4a2d-9c30-7b9e4f0a6c03",
                        "mediaKey": "721cb972-e7c0-43ae-8230-4518037eb9ae",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "One protocol connecting many tools. Photo: Alina Grubnyak on Unsplash."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "9dd71444-0933-4e01-8924-6db6f5a91f4d",
                "key": "dc6b448f-d52c-4b81-90bd-d52fa8b7cd60",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "quote",
                    "value": "Build the integration once, and every assistant can use it."
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "attribution",
                    "value": "The MCP promise"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "25b8da17-11eb-42e9-80f2-0df90950e32f",
                "key": "ed84097c-6e76-40cd-9bf5-e92ff46571f7",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "content",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<h2>Discover, don't hard-code</h2><p>An MCP server advertises its tools with names, descriptions and typed inputs. The assistant reads that menu at runtime, so adding a new capability means adding a tool to the server, not retraining or reprogramming anything on the client side.</p><p>It is the same idea that made USB successful: agree on the plug, and the ecosystem takes care of the rest.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "d8ea5283-f2de-4281-9241-c0173c057ac2",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "6c18757c-8a2a-452c-9136-b9b25eff8550",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "dc6b448f-d52c-4b81-90bd-d52fa8b7cd60",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "ed84097c-6e76-40cd-9bf5-e92ff46571f7",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "urls": [
