                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "content",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<h2>Safe by design</h2><p>Because every action goes through a named tool, you can see exactly what an assistant is allowed to do. Destructive steps can ask for confirmation, and editors keep the final say over what goes live.</p><p>That combination of real capability and clear guard rails is why MCP feels less like a gimmick and more like infrastructure.</p>",
